-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock (Affliction): Improved Drain Soul -- reconstruct the missing SQL
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- Same problem as woa_2026_08_06_06.sql: the DBC half of this talent was
-- applied straight to the live database and never got a tracked .sql file.
-- Nothing rewrites the talent itself, so on any fresh database Improved Drain
-- Soul keeps its stock threat
-- reduction, Effect2 stays empty, and
-- spell_warl_improved_drain_soul_shards_AuraScript reads a bonus of 0 and
-- returns before rolling -- a talent that loads, runs, and does nothing.
--
-- Rows dumped verbatim from the live table, not regenerated, so this is what
-- was actually being tested.
--
-- The design (see modules/world_of_alonecraft/src/WarlockDrainChanneling.cpp):
--   The threat reduction is gone -- threat is not the constraint in a solo
--   fork, the same reasoning that retired the threat halves of Destructive
--   Reach and Demonic Brutality.  In its place the talent raises Drain Soul's
--   Soul Shard generation rate by 50% / 100%.
--
--   EffectBasePoints2 49 / 99 with DieSides 1 gives CalcValue 50 / 100 --
--   the value the script reads via Effects[EFFECT_1].CalcValue(), and the
--   value $s2 renders in the tooltip.  One number, one source.
--   The mana-on-kill half is untouched.
-- ===========================================================================

DELETE FROM `alonecraft_spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (18213, 18372);
